                <note rend="inline" type="source">Doc. No. 13 bis (G).</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Amendment Proposed to the Clauses of the Draft Treaty
                        Concerning Bilateral Treaties</hi> (Art. 37.)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                        calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1946-10-15T23:59:59+01:00"
                        notBefore="1946-08-20T00:00:00+01:00">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 37</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Each Allied or Associated Power will notify Italy, within a period of 6
                        months of the coming into force of the present treaty, which pre-war
                        bilateral treaty it <hi rendition="#italic">does not</hi> desire to keep in
                        force or revive.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item><hi rendition="#italic">All treaties so notified are to be regarded as
                            abrogated</hi> within <hi rendition="#italic">one month from the date of
                            notification</hi>.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Any provisions <hi rendition="#italic">in treaties not so notified</hi>,
                        which are not in conformity with the present treaty, shall be
                        deleted.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>All treaties <hi rendition="#italic">not</hi> so notified will be
                        registered with the Secretariat of the United Nations in accordance with
                        Article 102 of the United Nations Charter.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
